  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Pinta IV was built in a modular fashion. Each section of the ship can
    be detached and has all the necessary components to travel and sustain a crew.
    This design was necessary to allow the crew to be more efficient while exploring
    other solar systems, as they can split up and continue their work independently.


    Every
    section has its own cockpit, engines, hibernation chambers and living quarters.


    The
    hibernation chambers have been modernized and adapted from their originally intended
    usage. Since the development of faster-than-light travel, their purpose was shifted
    from making extremely long journeys possible to protecting the crew members,
    as the process has shown to cause severe dizziness and physical fatigue.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
